  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "[\"Only one successful source view establishes this specimen exterior. Opposite surface and overall thickness inferred conservatively from rounded convolute shell; four renders are assessment views, not four photographed observations.\", \"Original shell-lip thin edge partly worn; do not restore an elaborate missing rim. Interior depth is unresolved by mineral preservation; retain only shallow observed recess and basal folds.\", \"Photo dimensions are approximate; aperture obliquity and shell edges limit precision. Palette is artistic fossil tan, not an original-life colour claim.\"] {\"unit\": \"metre\", \"height_Z\": 0.075, \"width_X\": 0.036, \"depth_Y_inferred\": 0.032, \"evidence\": \"Fig12 caption bars10mm. Render1172x1640: A bar x287–340=53px; body x142–333 about191px and y222–619 about397px; projected75×36mm. Depth32mm inferred, not measured.\", \"engineering_tolerance\": \"Height72–78mm, width34–39mm, inferred depth29–36mm. Design tolerances, not biological confidence intervals.\"}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：[\"Only one successful source view establishes this specimen exterior. Opposite surface and overall thickness inferred conservatively from rounded convolute shell; four renders are assessment views, not four photographed observations.\", \"Original shell-lip thin edge partly worn; do not restore an elaborate missing rim. Interior depth is unresolved by mineral preservation; retain only shallow observed recess and basal folds.\", \"Photo dimensions are approximate; aperture obliquity and shell edges limit precision. Palette is artistic fossil tan, not an original-life colour claim.\"] {\"unit\": \"metre\", \"height_Z\": 0.075, \"width_X\": 0.036, \"depth_Y_inferred\": 0.032, \"evidence\": \"Fig12 caption bars10mm. Render1172x1640: A bar x287–340=53px; body x142–333 about191px and y222–619 about397px; projected75×36mm. Depth32mm inferred, not measured.\", \"engineering_tolerance\": \"Height72–78mm, width34–39mm, inferred depth29–36mm. Design tolerances, not biological confidence intervals.\"}"
